Openshift is most used enterprise grade kubernetes platform in the market
    Note: Pod to Pod communication can be taken care by CNI(Container Network Interface)
          To run pods we need container run time and to keep pod secure we have Network policies
Problem with opensource kubernetes and advantage of Openshift?
   * Kubernetes is quite robust(strong/healthy) platform. It works very smooth and tested and used by lot of people.
   * there are 2 major things, that made organaziation to back out from k8s and search for Enterprise Grade K8S platform
   * Even though k8s is free and opensource. Anyone can download and install on their VM/physical server and use it. 
It has some disadvantage as below
   1. Lack of support. Lets say we encounter some issue with k8s cluster. it can be existing bug which has workaround but not sure how to implement it.
      or we might get any question related to scale up based on some scenario. we might get into any kind of question.
      For that we have to raise a issue in k8s github and wait for one of the k8s engineers/contributor to respond back. It may happen eventually 
      but it will take more time as its opensource community. Enterprise will not prefer thiss.
   2. Management overhead. Being an opensource project, k8s is not opiniated which means kubernetes will not tell you to use k8s only on ubuntu vm or 
      only on centos or on redhat vm. It will tell you the instructions, we have to install and manage it.
      Managing huge large scale appication in opensouce k8s is very difficult without support.
